  "Area": "Unclassified",
  "Number": 9,
  "Question": "The number of ounces of water needed to reduce \\(9\\) ounces of shaving lotion containing \\(50\\%\\) alcohol to a lotion containing \\(30\\%\\) alcohol is:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(3\\)",
    "B": "\\(4\\)",
    "C": "\\(5\\)",
    "D": "\\(6\\)",
    "E": "\\(7\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "Adding water increases the total amount of lotion but leaves the alcohol amount unchanged. Initially, the alcohol amount is\n\\[\n9(0.50)=4.5\\text{ ounces}.\n\\]\nThese 4.5 ounces must be 30% of the final total. Dividing the known part by its percentage gives that total:\n\\[\n4.5\\div0.30=15\\text{ ounces}.\n\\]\nThe water added is therefore \\(15-9=6\\) ounces, choice D.",
